.TH "UPKEEP" "1" "Sep 14, 2026" "1.7.1" "upkeep"
.SH NAME
upkeep \- upkeep v1.7.1
.sp
Portage update helper commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS upkeep
.sp
Maintain a Gentoo system.
.sp
\fB\-\-debug\fP is also accepted by every subcommand, so it may be given on either side of the
subcommand name.
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
upkeep [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.UNINDENT
.SS all
.sp
Sync, update, and clean in one pass.
.nf
\- \fBemerge \-\-sync\fP, wrapped by any configured \fB[sync]\fP hooks (skip with \fB\-\-no\-sync\fP)
\- everything \fBemerges\fP does, including the kernel upgrade
\- everything \fBecleans\fP does (skip with \fB\-\-no\-clean\fP)
.fi
.sp
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
upkeep all [OPTIONS]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-\-fatal\-upgrade\-kernel
Exit with status > 0 if kernel upgrade cannot be done.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-no\-clean
Skip the clean\-up stage.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-S, \-\-no\-sync
Skip synchronising the repositories.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-U, \-\-no\-upgrade\-kernel
Skip upgrading the kernel.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-ask
Pass \-\-ask to emerge.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config <config>
Override configuration file path.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-exclude <ATOM>
Atom to exclude from the @world update.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Pass \-\-verbose to emerge.
.UNINDENT
.SS ecleans
.sp
Remove build leftovers, unused packages, and stale distfiles.
.nf
\- Delete the contents of \fB${PORTAGE_TMPDIR}/portage\fP and any configured extra directories
\- \fBemerge \-\-depclean \-\-quiet\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-quiet @preserved\-rebuild\fP
\- \fBrevdep\-rebuild \-\-quiet\fP
\- \fBeclean\-dist \-\-deep\fP
\- \fBeclean\-pkg \-\-deep\fP
\- \fBemaint \-\-fix all\fP
\- Delete zero\-length files under \fBPKGDIR\fP
.fi
.sp
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
upkeep ecleans [OPTIONS]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config <config>
Override configuration file path.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.UNINDENT
.SS emerges
.sp
Update Portage, \fB@world\fP, and the kernel.
.nf
\- \fBemerge \-\-oneshot \-\-quiet \-\-update portage\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-keep\-going \-\-tree \-\-quiet \-\-update \-\-deep \-\-newuse \-\-with\-bdeps=y @world\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-usepkg=n \-\-keep\-going \-\-quiet @live\-rebuild\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-usepkg=n \-\-keep\-going \-\-quiet @preserved\-rebuild\fP
\- \fBsystemctl daemon\-reexec\fP if applicable
\- upgrade kernel
.fi
.sp
.sp
Anything listed under \fBextra_args\fP in the \fB[emerge]\fP table of the configuration file is
appended to the \fB@world\fP update.
.sp
