.SS rebuild\-kernel
.sp
Rebuild the kernel currently selected in \fB/usr/src/linux\fP\&.
.sp
Runs the build steps without touching the \fBeselect kernel\fP selection:
.nf
\- \fBmake oldconfig\fP, seeding \fB\&.config\fP from \fB/proc/config.gz\fP if needed
\- \fBmake\fP
\- \fBmake modules_install\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-keep\-going @module\-rebuild @x11\-module\-rebuild\fP
\- \fBmake install\fP
.fi
.sp
.sp
Usage
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
upkeep rebuild\-kernel [OPTIONS]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Options
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-number\-of\-jobs <number_of_jobs>
Number of tasks to run simultaneously.
.UNINDENT
.SS upgrade\-kernel
.sp
Select the newest kernel and build it.
.sp
\fBeselect kernel list\fP sorts its entries by version, so the highest\-numbered entry is the newest
kernel available. If it is already selected there is nothing to do. Otherwise:
.nf
\- \fBeselect kernel set\fP the newest entry
\- \fBmake oldconfig\fP, seeding \fB\&.config\fP from \fB/proc/config.gz\fP if needed
\- \fBmake\fP
\- \fBmake modules_install\fP
\- \fBemerge \-\-keep\-going @module\-rebuild @x11\-module\-rebuild\fP
\- \fBmake install\fP
.fi
.sp
.sp
